diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..1a44f28 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,21 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account settings
+
+Sign-in supports an explicit passkey button and conditional passkey autofill. Sign-up first creates a password-backed account, then offers optional platform passkey registration. `/devtools-times/account` supports passkey registration (including security keys), provider information, creation/last-used dates, renaming, deletion, and display-name changes. Sensitive changes require confirmation with the current account's passkey or password. Password sign-in remains available for recovery and unsupported browsers.
+
+The existing remote password service remains the authority for password registration and login. The local backend establishes a session only after that service accepts a password login; it never stores passwords or upstream tokens. Passkey authentication uses `@simplewebauthn/server` for challenge, origin, RP ID, signature, and counter validation. Challenges are session-bound, single-use, and expire after five minutes. Reauthentication requires user verification and credentials owned by the active account. Sessions use opaque, hashed-at-rest tokens in HttpOnly, SameSite cookies.
+
+Use Node **24+** (the database uses `node:sqlite`). Production must serve HTTPS and configure:
+
+- `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN`: the exact public origin, such as `https://news.example.com`, without a path. Defaults to the Astro `site` origin; localhost uses the incoming local origin.
+- `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID`: the relying-party domain, such as `news.example.com`. Defaults to the origin's hostname. Keep it stable after registering passkeys.
+- `AUTH_DB_PATH`: a persistent, writable SQLite path, such as `/var/lib/devtools-times/auth.sqlite`. Defaults to `./data/auth.sqlite`. Keep this database across restarts and deployments. This SQLite implementation is intended for a single application instance; multiple instances need a shared transactional store.
+
+The auth API enforces its own Origin checks because the sample globally disables Astro's origin checking. Registered passkeys are stored on the app's domain, independently of the remote password service. Changing a display name updates the local account and supported password managers; the password-service username stays unchanged.
+
+Client WebAuthn uses native browser APIs with the `webauthn-polyfills` JSON/capability compatibility layer. Optional Signal APIs synchronize accepted credential IDs and account display details without blocking successful operations. Provider names use a bundled snapshot of the [community AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids); common providers include their registry icons, with a generic icon/name fallback. AAGUID metadata is used only for display.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for isolated session/challenge/credential storage tests and `pnpm build` to compile. Neither command starts the application server.
